A||N||2||scarydok||Wanting to change 85 Fiero from 2.5 4-banger to 2.8L V-6...what do I need to change?||||1||
Z||000000||scarydok||12-04-2001||11:45 PM||||I have an 85 4 banger wanting to change to a 2.8 V-6...What do I need to change?  Still kinda new to the Fiero, just picked up my first one for $250 not running.  I'm pretty sure that I'll need to change the computer and wiring harness, and adjust the tach, but not sure what else that I'll need to change.  Please Help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Borgio||12-05-2001||12:56 AM||||I don't know what else you have to do to change to a 6. But as a suggestion, you could put a 3.4L in it. Pretty easy to get, and cheap, and a little extra power to work with.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||12-05-2001||04:06 PM||||Your best bet would be to have the donor car available.  You'll need (among other things) the fuel pump, ECM, wire harness, air cleaner assembly, accelerator cable, and the various odds and ends.  It saves a lot of time if you can have the donor car handy to get the various things you need.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
